The iOS 27.2 beta Apple released today removes the updated Health app that Apple was <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/16/ios-27-2-beta-health-app/">testing in earlier betas</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063937" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/apple-ios-27-health-app-watch.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" /><br/>
The removal of the Health app is not a surprise because Apple previously said the redesign <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-watch-series-12/">wouldn't be introduced until late 2026</a>. <br/>
<br/>
After upgrading to the fourth beta, the Health app has a popup that says the new app features will come in a future update. Data collected during the beta remains available in the Settings app. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-health-app-later.jpg" alt="" width="2290" height="1288" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070692" /><br/>
